            <ArticleTitle>Simultaneous occurrence of ovarian torsion and gangrenous strangulation through a congenital opening in the mesosalpinx.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>290-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of simultaneous occurrence of ovarian torsion and gangrenous strangulation through a congenital opening in the mesosalpinx is presented. This case closely resembles that of intestinal strangulation through a mesosalpingeal defect, which is also very rare. 1) The condition was recognized at laparotomy performed for symptoms and signs of &quot;an acute abdomen&quot;; 2) the patient was a pregnant woman; 3) the final outcome was good after prompt surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
